;; The known disagreements of the per-form differential check (bin/diffcheck,
;; doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, "F2 as built"): it passes when the disagreeing cases are
;; exactly these. Rewritten by bin/diffcheck --write-expected, which keeps the reasons
;; of the cases still disagreeing; edit the reasons by hand.
{:impl "bin/diffcheck"
 :about "Clojure's pair: a corpus evaluated (the evaluator) against compiled (arbace.c2j, j2g). The Java forms' pair: interpreted (arbace.classes.interp) against translated (j2g). Found on 2026-10-17 besides these, and fixed in arbace.c2j.emit: import's value (nil compiled, the class evaluated and on the JVM: 21 cases, definterface's among them) and a deftype in a fn's code (its methods' this emitted as the fn's self: every compiled defrecord failed j2g's analysis)."
 :mismatches
 [{:reason "Clojure's pair, compilation's semantics, as the JVM's AOT: compiled code makes the vars it names when its constants are made, when the namespace's loader starts (Compiler$AOT/pool), so fresh.ns/fv and scratch.space/in-scratch are interned before the cases that intern or define them run, and user/map, which a later (def map 1) defines, replaces arbace.core/map's mapping in user before (resolve 'map); evaluated code interns a var when the form naming it is analyzed"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:453" :form "(count (ns-publics 'fresh.ns))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:454" :form "(count (ns-map 'fresh.ns))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:470" :form "(arbace.core/count (arbace.core/ns-publics 'scratch.space))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:480" :form "(resolve 'map)"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, not reproducible: an identity hash (StringBuilder's), different in each run (the oracle's known mismatch of the same case)"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/strings.ae:408" :form "(hash (StringBuilder. \"x\"))"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, a position in a message: eval at run time of a form without positions reports Compiler/LINE and COLUMN, which Compiler.load sets for each top-level form of an evaluated namespace but a compiled loader does not (Compiler$AOT/load, as the JVM's __init class), so the compiled run names the position of the form that loaded the namespace (the harness's, 1:33)"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/harvest/vars.ae:5" :form "(eval (arbace.core/seq (arbace.core/concat (arbace.core/list (quote binding)) (arbace.core/list (arb..."}]}

  {:reason "The Java forms' pair, the interpreter's known limits (test/j2g/record_fixtures.ae: the fixtures are recorded on the JVM because of them): a class of Java forms made at run time cannot extend java.io.StringReader (FxCode) nor reach java.lang.invoke's MethodHandles (FxVarHandles, test/j2g/fixtures:10 since FxJn7 came before it, JN7); j2g translates both. The fixtures' calls of the classes the interpreter could not define then reach the compiled classes in both runs, and agree"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/j2g/fixtures:2" :form "(load-file \"test/j2g/fixtures/FxCode.ae\")"}
    {:case "test/j2g/fixtures:10" :form "(load-file \"test/j2g/fixtures/FxVarHandles.ae\")"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, the compiled constants (SA155), decided (F3.3 (a), 2026-10-17, the user): a class's symbols without metadata are made once in its constant pool and named by the constants that hold them, so two equal quoted symbols of compiled code are identical; the evaluator and the JVM make one symbol per constant (Clojure leaves symbols' identity unspecified). Found once the corpora's user stayed user (dcf.user, made bare by in-ns, had no identical?)"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:597" :form "(identical? 'a 'a)"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, native.ae's copy (c2j:), by design of the evaluator (doc/go/EVAL-PLAN.md Q1; the oracle's known mismatch of the same cases, known-go-amd64-frozen.edn): a ^long fn the Java forms compiler compiles is, interpreted, a fn made at run time, one Go type calling invoke, so it is no IFn$LL or IFn$LOL; compiled (its class in the back end's tree, translated by j2g) it implements them, as on the JVM, whose answers the compiled run gives"
   :cases
   [{:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:233" :form "(.invokePrim ^arbace.lang.IFn$LL sq 6)"}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:234" :form "(instance? arbace.lang.IFn$LOL mixed)"}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:237" :form "(let [f (fn ^long [^long x] (java-str x) (inc x))] [(f 1) (instance? arbace.lang.IFn$LL f)])"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, native.ae's copy (c2j:), a limit of j2g left by F2.4: the Java forms compiler's class of a deftype or fn whose Clojure code names the namespace's vars (->Ext in Mutual's area, named in its own body) or holds a deftype* (in-fn, class-forms-in-methods, record-in-fn: the Java forms compiler at run time, user.InFn) is in the back end's tree, but j2g's analysis, without the namespace's vars and compiler, fails and leaves it out (j2g's report, :analysis-failures; the cases of jforms-excluded.edn's dcf.defclass.Clj and native.nested_deftype.Host); the compiled code naming it fails where it runs (ClassNotFoundException, \"j2g: class ... is not in the closed world\"; arbace.c2j.emit/*late-classes*: the namespace still loads), and the cases calling those fns find them unbound"
   :cases
   [{:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:157" :form "(deftype Mutual [^:unsynchronized-mutable cnt]\n  Shape\n  (area [this] (set! cnt (inc cnt)) (label :l..."}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:161" :form "[(area (->Ext 3)) (area (scaled (->Ext 3) 2)) (area (->Mutual 0)) (scaled (->Mutual 5) 3)\n (satisfie..."}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:175" :form "(defn named [n] (switch (int n) 0 0 (+ n (named (dec n)))))"}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:182" :form "(named 4)"}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:418" :form "(defn- in-fn [n]\n  (deftype InFn [^long a b] Object (toString [this] (str \"InFn\" a b)))\n  (switch (i..."}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:421" :form "(defn- class-forms-in-methods [n]\n  (deftype WithForms [^long a]\n    Object\n    (toString [this] (la..."}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:426" :form "(defn- record-in-fn []\n  (label :l (defrecord RecInFn [x ^long y]\n              Comparable (compareT..."}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:437" :form "[(in-fn 0) (in-fn 5)]"}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:438" :form "(native.nested_deftype.InFn/getBasis)"}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:439" :form "(class-forms-in-methods 3)"}
    {:case "c2j:test/oracle/forms/native.ae:440" :form "(let [r (record-in-fn)] [(into {} r) (.compareTo ^Comparable r nil) (.getName (class r))])"}]}]}
